-- =====================================================================================================================
-- CASE W1. Pre-injury average weekly earnings (Sch 3 cl 2; Regulation cl 8AB) and indexation (ss 82A, 82C).
-- =====================================================================================================================

-- $65,000 over 52 weeks: 65000 / 52 = $1,250.
#ASSERT `What are my pre-injury average weekly earnings` 65000 52 EQUALS 1250
-- Started the job 26 weeks before (Regulation cl 8B shortens the period): $26,000 / 26 = $1,000.
#ASSERT `What are my pre-injury average weekly earnings` 26000 26 EQUALS 1000
-- $5,000 over 52 weeks = $96.15..., below the $155 minimum, so $155 (cl 2(4), cl 8AB).
#ASSERT `What are my pre-injury average weekly earnings` 5000 52 EQUALS 155
-- Review date with a declared factor of 1.02: 1250 x 1.02 = $1,275.
#ASSERT `What are my pre-injury average weekly earnings after the review date` 1250 1.02 EQUALS 1275
-- A factor below 1 would reduce the amount: the variation does not take effect (s 82C(a)).
#ASSERT `What are my pre-injury average weekly earnings after the review date` 1250 0.99 EQUALS 1250

-- =====================================================================================================================
-- CASE W2. Current weekly earnings (Sch 3 cl 8): the greater of actual earnings and what the worker is able to earn.
-- =====================================================================================================================

#ASSERT `What are my current weekly earnings` 300 500 EQUALS 500
#ASSERT `What are my current weekly earnings` 600 400 EQUALS 600

-- =====================================================================================================================
-- CASE W3. Workers with high needs and highest needs (s 32A). Answers: permanent impairment; assessed; degree; pending
-- for MMI; insurer satisfied over 20%; (highest needs only) insurer satisfied over 30%.
-- =====================================================================================================================

-- Assessed at 25%: high needs (more than 20%), not highest (not more than 30%).
#ASSERT `Am I a worker with high needs` TRUE TRUE 25 FALSE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I a worker with highest needs` TRUE TRUE 25 FALSE FALSE)
-- Assessed at 35%: both.
#ASSERT `Am I a worker with highest needs` TRUE TRUE 35 FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `Am I a worker with high needs` TRUE TRUE 35 FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- Assessed at exactly 20%: not "more than 20%".
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I a worker with high needs` TRUE TRUE 20 FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- Assessed at 15%, but the insurer is satisfied it is likely more than 20%: para (c) is not limited to unassessed workers.
#ASSERT `Am I a worker with high needs` TRUE TRUE 15 FALSE TRUE FALSE
-- Not assessed, the assessor declined for lack of MMI: para (b) of both definitions, with no threshold (finding 5).
#ASSERT `Am I a worker with high needs` TRUE FALSE 0 TRUE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `Am I a worker with highest needs` TRUE FALSE 0 TRUE FALSE
-- Once assessed (at 25%), para (b) "no longer applies": not highest needs, even with the pending flag still set.
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I a worker with highest needs` TRUE TRUE 25 TRUE FALSE)
-- No permanent impairment: neither.
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I a worker with high needs` FALSE FALSE 0 TRUE TRUE TRUE)

-- =====================================================================================================================
-- CASE W4. The entitlement periods (s 32A; ss 36-39).
-- =====================================================================================================================

#ASSERT `Which entitlement period is this week in` 1 EQUALS `the first entitlement period (weeks 1 to 13)`
#ASSERT `Which entitlement period is this week in` 13 EQUALS `the first entitlement period (weeks 1 to 13)`
#ASSERT `Which entitlement period is this week in` 14 EQUALS `the second entitlement period (weeks 14 to 130)`
#ASSERT `Which entitlement period is this week in` 130 EQUALS `the second entitlement period (weeks 14 to 130)`
#ASSERT `Which entitlement period is this week in` 131 EQUALS `after the second entitlement period (weeks 131 to 260)`
#ASSERT `Which entitlement period is this week in` 260 EQUALS `after the second entitlement period (weeks 131 to 260)`
#ASSERT `Which entitlement period is this week in` 261 EQUALS `after 260 weeks`
#ASSERT `In which week does my current entitlement period end` 5 EQUALS 13
#ASSERT `In which week does my current entitlement period end` 14 EQUALS 130
#ASSERT `In which week does my current entitlement period end` 200 EQUALS 260

-- =====================================================================================================================
-- CASE W5. The retiring age (s 52). Answers: day of injury; day the worker reaches pension age; day of first incapacity.
-- =====================================================================================================================

-- Injured 1 March 2024, before reaching pension age on 15 June 2030: payments stop after the first anniversary,
-- 15 June 2031 (s 52(2)(a)).
#ASSERT `What is the last day my weekly payments can cover because of my age` `1 Mar 2024` `15 Jun 2030` `1 Mar 2024` EQUALS `15 Jun 2031`
-- Injured 1 March 2024, after reaching pension age on 10 January 2024; first incapacity 4 March 2024: 12 months after
-- it, 4 March 2025 (s 52(2)(b)).
#ASSERT `What is the last day my weekly payments can cover because of my age` `1 Mar 2024` `10 Jan 2024` `4 Mar 2024` EQUALS `4 Mar 2025`
-- Injured on the day of reaching pension age: "on or after reaching the retiring age", so (b); first incapacity the same
-- day: 10 January 2025.
#ASSERT `What is the last day my weekly payments can cover because of my age` `10 Jan 2024` `10 Jan 2024` `10 Jan 2024` EQUALS `10 Jan 2025`
-- Pension age reached on 29 February 2028: first anniversary read as 28 February 2029 (READING).
#ASSERT `What is the last day my weekly payments can cover because of my age` `1 Mar 2024` `29 Feb 2028` `1 Mar 2024` EQUALS `28 Feb 2029`

-- =====================================================================================================================
-- CASE W6. After week 130 (s 38). Answers: no CWC indefinitely; CWC; applied in writing; weeks left when applied; hours;
-- current weekly earnings; indefinitely unable to earn more; then the s 32A facts (permanent impairment; assessed;
-- degree; pending for MMI; insurer satisfied over 20%; insurer satisfied over 30%), from which "worker with high needs"
-- is worked out; the s 38(3)(b) amount if known. "Not high needs" below is assessed at 15% (not more than 20%, nothing
-- pending, the insurer not satisfied of more); "high needs" is assessed at 25% (s 32A para (a)).
-- =====================================================================================================================

#ASSERT `Am I entitled to weekly payments after week 130` TRUE FALSE FALSE 0 0 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE NOTHING EQUALS `entitled after week 130: no current work capacity, likely to continue indefinitely (s 38(2))`
-- CWC, not high needs; applied with 40 weeks left; 20 hours; $600; assessed unable to earn more: s 38(3).
#ASSERT `Am I entitled to weekly payments after week 130` FALSE TRUE TRUE 40 20 600 TRUE TRUE TRUE 15 FALSE FALSE FALSE NOTHING EQUALS `entitled after week 130: the s 38(3) conditions are met`
-- Applied with 60 weeks left: earlier than 52 weeks before the end (s 38(3)(a)).
#ASSERT NOT (`is entitled after week 130` (`Am I entitled to weekly payments after week 130` FALSE TRUE TRUE 60 20 600 TRUE TRUE TRUE 15 FALSE FALSE FALSE NOTHING))
-- 12 hours a week: under 15 (s 38(3)(b)).
#ASSERT NOT (`is entitled after week 130` (`Am I entitled to weekly payments after week 130` FALSE TRUE TRUE 40 12 600 TRUE TRUE TRUE 15 FALSE FALSE FALSE NOTHING))
-- $160 a week meets the $155 of the deposited text, but not a declared $250.
#ASSERT `is entitled after week 130` (`Am I entitled to weekly payments after week 130` FALSE TRUE TRUE 40 20 160 TRUE TRUE TRUE 15 FALSE FALSE FALSE NOTHING)
#ASSERT NOT (`is entitled after week 130` (`Am I entitled to weekly payments after week 130` FALSE TRUE TRUE 40 20 160 TRUE TRUE TRUE 15 FALSE FALSE FALSE (JUST 250)))
-- Not assessed as indefinitely unable to earn more (s 38(3)(c)).
#ASSERT NOT (`is entitled after week 130` (`Am I entitled to weekly payments after week 130` FALSE TRUE TRUE 40 20 600 FALSE TRUE TRUE 15 FALSE FALSE FALSE NOTHING))
-- High needs, CWC, applied with 10 weeks left, not working: s 38(3A) asks only for the application.
#ASSERT `Am I entitled to weekly payments after week 130` FALSE TRUE TRUE 10 0 0 FALSE TRUE TRUE 25 FALSE FALSE FALSE NOTHING EQUALS `entitled after week 130: a worker with high needs with current work capacity who applied in time (s 38(3A))`
-- High needs, but no application.
#ASSERT NOT (`is entitled after week 130` (`Am I entitled to weekly payments after week 130` FALSE TRUE FALSE 0 0 0 FALSE TRUE TRUE 25 FALSE FALSE FALSE NOTHING))
-- Applied after the end of the second entitlement period (0 weeks left): the text sets no latest day (finding 7).
#ASSERT `is entitled after week 130` (`Am I entitled to weekly payments after week 130` FALSE TRUE TRUE 0 0 0 FALSE TRUE TRUE 25 FALSE FALSE FALSE NOTHING)
-- No assessment either way.
#ASSERT NOT (`is entitled after week 130` (`Am I entitled to weekly payments after week 130` FALSE FALSE TRUE 10 20 600 TRUE TRUE TRUE 15 FALSE FALSE FALSE NOTHING))
-- High needs worked out from s 32A (finding 16): not assessed, the assessor declined for lack of MMI (para (b)), applied
-- with 10 weeks left, not working: s 38(3A).
#ASSERT `Am I entitled to weekly payments after week 130` FALSE TRUE TRUE 10 0 0 FALSE TRUE FALSE 0 TRUE FALSE FALSE NOTHING EQUALS `entitled after week 130: a worker with high needs with current work capacity who applied in time (s 38(3A))`
-- Assessed at 15%, but the insurer is satisfied it is likely more than 20% (para (c)): high needs, so s 38(3A).
#ASSERT `Am I entitled to weekly payments after week 130` FALSE TRUE TRUE 10 0 0 FALSE TRUE TRUE 15 FALSE TRUE FALSE NOTHING EQUALS `entitled after week 130: a worker with high needs with current work capacity who applied in time (s 38(3A))`
-- Assessed at exactly 20%: not "more than 20%", so not high needs; not working, so s 38(3)(b) is not met.
#ASSERT NOT (`is entitled after week 130` (`Am I entitled to weekly payments after week 130` FALSE TRUE TRUE 10 0 0 FALSE TRUE TRUE 20 FALSE FALSE FALSE NOTHING))

-- =====================================================================================================================
-- CASE W7. After 260 weeks (s 39): only an assessed degree of more than 20%.
-- =====================================================================================================================

#ASSERT `Can my weekly payments continue after 260 weeks` TRUE TRUE 21
#ASSERT NOT (`Can my weekly payments continue after 260 weeks` TRUE TRUE 20)
#ASSERT NOT (`Can my weekly payments continue after 260 weeks` TRUE FALSE 0)

-- =====================================================================================================================
-- CASE W8. The weekly payment (ss 33-38A, 39, 52). Injured 1 March 2024, not a set-apart class; pension age reached
-- 15 June 2030; first incapacity 1 March 2024; the week asked about includes 3 June 2024 unless stated. Deposited
-- figures: maximum $1,838.70 (s 34(1)), s 38A amount $788.32.
-- Helper answers: week; work capacity; PIAWE; actual earnings; able to earn; hours; entitled after 130; assessed; degree.
-- =====================================================================================================================

GIVEN `w` IS A NUMBER, `cap` IS A `Work capacity`, `piawe` IS A NUMBER, `actual` IS A NUMBER, `able` IS A NUMBER, `hours` IS A NUMBER, `after 130` IS A BOOLEAN, `assessed` IS A BOOLEAN, `degree` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Weekly payment`
`case W8` `w` `cap` `piawe` `actual` `able` `hours` `after 130` `assessed` `degree` MEANS
    `How much is my weekly payment this week` `1 Mar 2024` `not set apart` `w` `cap` `piawe` `actual` `able` `hours` NOTHING NOTHING `assessed` `assessed` `degree` FALSE FALSE `after 130` `15 Jun 2030` `1 Mar 2024` `3 Jun 2024`

-- (a) Week 5, no current work capacity, PIAWE $1,500: 95% = $1,425 (s 36(1)).
#ASSERT `case W8` 5 `no current work capacity` 1500 0 0 0 FALSE FALSE 0 EQUALS `a weekly payment of` 1425 "s 36(1)"
-- (b) PIAWE $2,500: 95% = $2,375, capped at the maximum $1,838.70 (s 34(1AA)).
#ASSERT `case W8` 5 `no current work capacity` 2500 0 0 0 FALSE FALSE 0 EQUALS `a weekly payment of` 1838.70 "s 36(1)"
-- (c) Week 5, current work capacity, earns $300 but able to earn $500, so current weekly earnings $500: the lesser of
-- 1425 - 500 = 925 and 1838.70 - 500 = 1338.70 is $925 (s 36(2)).
#ASSERT `case W8` 5 `current work capacity` 1500 300 500 10 FALSE FALSE 0 EQUALS `a weekly payment of` 925 "s 36(2)"
-- (d) PIAWE $2,500, current weekly earnings $500: the lesser of 2375 - 500 = 1875 and 1338.70 is $1,338.70.
#ASSERT `case W8` 5 `current work capacity` 2500 500 0 10 FALSE FALSE 0 EQUALS `a weekly payment of` 1338.70 "s 36(2)"
-- (e) Week 20, no current work capacity: 80% of $1,500 = $1,200 (s 37(1)).
#ASSERT `case W8` 20 `no current work capacity` 1500 0 0 0 FALSE FALSE 0 EQUALS `a weekly payment of` 1200 "s 37(1)"
-- (f) Week 20, current work capacity, 20 hours, $600: the lesser of 1425 - 600 = 825 and 1238.70 is $825 (s 37(2)).
#ASSERT `case W8` 20 `current work capacity` 1500 600 0 20 FALSE FALSE 0 EQUALS `a weekly payment of` 825 "s 37(2)"
-- (g) Week 20, current work capacity, 10 hours, $400: the lesser of 1200 - 400 = 800 and 1438.70 is $800 (s 37(3)).
#ASSERT `case W8` 20 `current work capacity` 1500 400 0 10 FALSE FALSE 0 EQUALS `a weekly payment of` 800 "s 37(3)"
-- (g2) Exactly 15 hours is "not less than 15 hours": 95%, so 1425 - 400 = $1,025 (s 37(2)).
#ASSERT `case W8` 20 `current work capacity` 1500 400 0 15 FALSE FALSE 0 EQUALS `a weekly payment of` 1025 "s 37(2)"
-- (h) Week 140, no current work capacity, entitled under s 38: 80% = $1,200 (s 38(6)).
#ASSERT `case W8` 140 `no current work capacity` 1500 0 0 0 TRUE FALSE 0 EQUALS `a weekly payment of` 1200 "s 38(6)"
-- (i) Week 140, current work capacity, $600: the lesser of 1200 - 600 = 600 and 1238.70 is $600 (s 38(7)).
#ASSERT `case W8` 140 `current work capacity` 1500 600 0 20 TRUE FALSE 0 EQUALS `a weekly payment of` 600 "s 38(7)"
-- (j) Week 140, not entitled under s 38: nothing (s 38(1)).
#ASSERT `case W8` 140 `no current work capacity` 1500 0 0 0 FALSE FALSE 0 EQUALS `no weekly payment` `the second entitlement period has ended and s 38 does not continue the payments (s 38(1))`
-- (k) Week 270, entitled under s 38, impairment not assessed: nothing (s 39(1)).
#ASSERT `case W8` 270 `no current work capacity` 1500 0 0 0 TRUE FALSE 0 EQUALS `no weekly payment` `260 weeks of weekly payments have been paid or are payable, and the impairment is not assessed at more than 20% (s 39)`
-- (l) Week 270, assessed at 25%, entitled under s 38: s 39(2) lets it go on: 80% = $1,200 (s 38(6)).
#ASSERT `case W8` 270 `no current work capacity` 1500 0 0 0 TRUE TRUE 25 EQUALS `a weekly payment of` 1200 "s 38(6)"
-- (m) Highest needs (assessed 35%), week 140, current weekly earnings $1,100: the lesser of 1200 - 1100 = 100 and
-- 738.70 is $100, below $788.32, so $788.32 (s 38A(1)).
#ASSERT `case W8` 140 `current work capacity` 1500 1100 0 30 TRUE TRUE 35 EQUALS `a weekly payment of` 788.32 "s 38(7), raised to the s 38A amount"
-- (n) Highest needs, current weekly earnings $1,300: 1200 - 1300 is below nil, so nil; s 38A read literally raises it to
-- $788.32 (finding 6).
#ASSERT `case W8` 140 `current work capacity` 1500 1300 0 30 TRUE TRUE 35 EQUALS `a weekly payment of` 788.32 "s 38(7), raised to the s 38A amount"
-- (o) Not highest needs, current weekly earnings $1,300 in week 20 with 10 hours: 1200 - 1300 below nil, so nil.
#ASSERT `case W8` 20 `current work capacity` 1500 1300 0 10 FALSE FALSE 0 EQUALS `a weekly payment of` 0 "s 37(3)"
-- (p) No incapacity for work: nothing (s 33).
#ASSERT `case W8` 5 `no incapacity for work` 1500 1500 0 38 FALSE FALSE 0 EQUALS `no weekly payment` `there is no incapacity for work (s 33)`
-- (q) PIAWE of $100 is taken to be $155: 95% of 155 = $147.25 (Sch 3 cl 2(4), Regulation cl 8AB; s 36(1)).
#ASSERT `case W8` 5 `no current work capacity` 100 0 0 0 FALSE FALSE 0 EQUALS `a weekly payment of` 147.25 "s 36(1)"
-- (r) A declared maximum of $2,000 instead of the deposited $1,838.70: PIAWE $2,500, 95% = 2375, capped at $2,000.
#ASSERT `How much is my weekly payment this week` `1 Mar 2024` `not set apart` 5 `no current work capacity` 2500 0 0 0 (JUST 2000) NOTHING FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE `15 Jun 2030` `1 Mar 2024` `3 Jun 2024` EQUALS `a weekly payment of` 2000 "s 36(1)"
-- (s) The retiring age: last day 15 June 2031 (case W5). A week including 15 June 2031 is paid; one including 20 June
-- 2031 is not (s 52(2)(a)).
#ASSERT `How much is my weekly payment this week` `1 Mar 2024` `not set apart` 140 `no current work capacity` 1500 0 0 0 NOTHING NOTHING FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE TRUE `15 Jun 2030` `1 Mar 2024` `15 Jun 2031` EQUALS `a weekly payment of` 1200 "s 38(6)"
#ASSERT `How much is my weekly payment this week` `1 Mar 2024` `not set apart` 140 `no current work capacity` 1500 0 0 0 NOTHING NOTHING FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE TRUE `15 Jun 2030` `1 Mar 2024` `20 Jun 2031` EQUALS `no weekly payment` `the incapacity falls after the last day s 52 allows, because of the retiring age`
-- (t) Not covered: injured 1 October 2019, before 21 October 2019; and a police officer.
#ASSERT `How much is my weekly payment this week` `1 Oct 2019` `not set apart` 5 `no current work capacity` 1500 0 0 0 NOTHING NOTHING FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE `15 Jun 2030` `1 Oct 2019` `3 Jun 2024` EQUALS `the weekly payment is not covered` `the injury was received before 21 October 2019: Regulation Part 3 and the Schedule 6 transitional provisions apply, which this encoding does not cover`
#ASSERT `How much is my weekly payment this week` `1 Mar 2024` `a police officer, paramedic or firefighter` 5 `no current work capacity` 1500 0 0 0 NOTHING NOTHING FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE `15 Jun 2030` `1 Mar 2024` `3 Jun 2024` EQUALS `the weekly payment is not covered` `the worker is a police officer, paramedic or firefighter: Schedule 6 keeps the 2012, 2015 and 2018 amendments from the injury, and the earlier law is not deposited`

-- =====================================================================================================================
-- CASE W9. Medical expenses (s 59A). Injured 1 March 2024. Helper answers: kind; surgery consequential; approved in 2
-- years; then the s 32A facts (permanent impairment; assessed; degree; pending for MMI; insurer satisfied over 20%;
-- insurer satisfied over 30%), from which "worker with high needs" (s 59A(5)) is worked out; weekly payments had; still
-- payable; claim first made; weekly payments ceased.
-- =====================================================================================================================

GIVEN `kind` IS A `Treatment kind`, `consequential` IS A BOOLEAN, `approved` IS A BOOLEAN, `impairment` IS A BOOLEAN, `assessed` IS A BOOLEAN, `degree` IS A NUMBER, `pending` IS A BOOLEAN, `over 20` IS A BOOLEAN, `over 30` IS A BOOLEAN, `had weekly` IS A BOOLEAN, `still payable` IS A BOOLEAN, `claim day` IS A DATE, `ceased day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Medical compensation period`
`case W9` `kind` `consequential` `approved` `impairment` `assessed` `degree` `pending` `over 20` `over 30` `had weekly` `still payable` `claim day` `ceased day` MEANS
    `For how long will my medical expenses be paid` `1 Mar 2024` `not set apart` `kind` `consequential` `approved` `impairment` `assessed` `degree` `pending` `over 20` `over 30` `had weekly` `still payable` `claim day` `ceased day`

-- Weekly payments ceased 31 December 2025, not assessed: 2 years commencing that day, so the last day is 30 December 2027.
#ASSERT `case W9` `other treatment, service or assistance` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE `10 Apr 2024` `31 Dec 2025` EQUALS `payable for treatment given up to and including` `30 Dec 2027` 2
-- Assessed at 8%, and at exactly 10%: "10% or less": still 2 years (s 59A(2)(a)).
#ASSERT `case W9` `other treatment, service or assistance` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE 8 FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE `10 Apr 2024` `31 Dec 2025` EQUALS `payable for treatment given up to and including` `30 Dec 2027` 2
#ASSERT `case W9` `other treatment, service or assistance` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE 10 FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE `10 Apr 2024` `31 Dec 2025` EQUALS `payable for treatment given up to and including` `30 Dec 2027` 2
-- Assessed at 15%, and at exactly 20%: "more than 10% but not more than 20%": 5 years, to 30 December 2030 (s 59A(2)(b)).
-- At 20% the worker is not one with high needs ("more than 20%", s 32A para (a)).
#ASSERT `case W9` `other treatment, service or assistance` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE 15 FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE `10 Apr 2024` `31 Dec 2025` EQUALS `payable for treatment given up to and including` `30 Dec 2030` 5
#ASSERT `case W9` `other treatment, service or assistance` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE 20 FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE `10 Apr 2024` `31 Dec 2025` EQUALS `payable for treatment given up to and including` `30 Dec 2030` 5
-- No weekly payments ever: 2 years from the claim, 10 April 2024, so to 9 April 2026.
#ASSERT `case W9` `other treatment, service or assistance` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `10 Apr 2024` `31 Dec 2025` EQUALS `payable for treatment given up to and including` `9 Apr 2026` 2
-- Weekly payments still payable: the period has not begun.
#ASSERT `case W9` `other treatment, service or assistance` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE `10 Apr 2024` `31 Dec 2025` EQUALS `the compensation period has not begun: it will run for this many years from the day weekly payments cease (s 59A(2))` 2
-- Assessed at 25%, the insurer not satisfied of anything more: a worker with high needs under s 32A para (a), so no limit
-- (s 59A(5)). Before finding 16 the seat asked "high needs" as a separate yes or no, and "no" gave 5 years to 30 December
-- 2030; s 59A(2)(b) stops at 20%.
#ASSERT `case W9` `other treatment, service or assistance` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE 25 FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE `10 Apr 2024` `31 Dec 2025` EQUALS `no time limit: s 59A does not apply to a worker with high needs (s 59A(5))`
-- Assessed at 15%, but the insurer is satisfied it is likely more than 20%: high needs (s 32A para (c)), no limit.
#ASSERT `case W9` `other treatment, service or assistance` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE 15 FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE `10 Apr 2024` `31 Dec 2025` EQUALS `no time limit: s 59A does not apply to a worker with high needs (s 59A(5))`
-- Not assessed, the assessor declined for lack of MMI: high needs (s 32A para (b)), no limit, although s 39 would stop
-- weekly payments at 260 weeks (case W7; finding 9).
#ASSERT `case W9` `other treatment, service or assistance` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE 0 TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE `10 Apr 2024` `31 Dec 2025` EQUALS `no time limit: s 59A does not apply to a worker with high needs (s 59A(5))`
-- Not assessed, the insurer satisfied it is likely more than 30%: highest needs, which "high needs" includes; no limit.
#ASSERT `case W9` `other treatment, service or assistance` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE `10 Apr 2024` `31 Dec 2025` EQUALS `no time limit: s 59A does not apply to a worker with high needs (s 59A(5))`
-- Contradictory facts: no permanent impairment, yet a degree assessed at 25%. Not high needs (s 32A needs permanent
-- impairment), and s 59A(2) states no compensation period above 20%: the explicit answer, not 5 years.
#ASSERT `case W9` `other treatment, service or assistance` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE 25 FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE `10 Apr 2024` `31 Dec 2025` EQUALS `no compensation period: s 59A(2) states none for a degree assessed at more than 20% (s 32A makes such a worker one with high needs, s 59A(5))`
-- Hearing aids: no limit (s 59A(6)(a)); a home modification likewise (s 59A(6)(b)).
#ASSERT `case W9` `crutches, artificial members, eyes or teeth, or other artificial aids or spectacles (including hearing aids and batteries)` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE `10 Apr 2024` `31 Dec 2025` EQUALS `no time limit for this kind of treatment (s 59A(6))`
#ASSERT `case W9` `the modification of the worker's home or vehicle` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE `10 Apr 2024` `31 Dec 2025` EQUALS `no time limit for this kind of treatment (s 59A(6))`
-- Secondary surgery (consequential, approved within 2 years): no limit (s 59A(6)(c), (7)). Surgery that is not
-- consequential on earlier surgery: the ordinary period.
#ASSERT `case W9` `surgery` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE `10 Apr 2024` `31 Dec 2025` EQUALS `no time limit for this kind of treatment (s 59A(6))`
#ASSERT `case W9` `surgery` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE `10 Apr 2024` `31 Dec 2025` EQUALS `payable for treatment given up to and including` `30 Dec 2027` 2
-- Treatment on the last day, 30 December 2027, is paid; on 31 December 2027 it is not, unless weekly payments are
-- payable for that day again (s 59A(3)).
#ASSERT `Will my treatment on this day be paid for` `1 Mar 2024` `not set apart` `other treatment, service or assistance` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE `10 Apr 2024` `31 Dec 2025` `30 Dec 2027` FALSE EQUALS `compensation is payable for treatment on that day`
#ASSERT `Will my treatment on this day be paid for` `1 Mar 2024` `not set apart` `other treatment, service or assistance` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE `10 Apr 2024` `31 Dec 2025` `31 Dec 2027` FALSE EQUALS `not payable: the treatment is after the compensation period ended (s 59A(1))`
#ASSERT `Will my treatment on this day be paid for` `1 Mar 2024` `not set apart` `other treatment, service or assistance` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE `10 Apr 2024` `31 Dec 2025` `31 Dec 2027` TRUE EQUALS `compensation is payable for treatment on that day, as weekly payments are payable again (s 59A(3))`
-- Assessed at 25% (high needs): treatment on 31 December 2030, the day after a 15% worker's 5 years end, is paid for.
#ASSERT `Will my treatment on this day be paid for` `1 Mar 2024` `not set apart` `other treatment, service or assistance` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE 25 FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE `10 Apr 2024` `31 Dec 2025` `31 Dec 2030` FALSE EQUALS `compensation is payable for treatment on that day`
