-- =====================================================================================================================
-- CASE W12. Notice of injury (1998 Act s 254). Answers: as soon as possible; before leaving voluntarily; special
-- circumstance.
-- =====================================================================================================================

#ASSERT `Can I still recover compensation given my notice of injury` TRUE TRUE `no special circumstance` EQUALS `notice of injury is no bar: it was given as soon as possible and before the worker left the employment (s 254(1))`
#ASSERT `Can I still recover compensation given my notice of injury` FALSE TRUE `no special circumstance` EQUALS `compensation is not recoverable: notice was not given as s 254(1) requires, and no special circumstance applies`
#ASSERT `Can I still recover compensation given my notice of injury` FALSE TRUE `the employer knew of the injury at or about the time it happened (s 254(3)(c))` EQUALS `the failure is no bar, if the special circumstance is found in proceedings (s 254(2))`
-- Told the employer promptly but only after leaving the job voluntarily: s 254(1) is not met.
#ASSERT `Can I still recover compensation given my notice of injury` TRUE FALSE `no special circumstance` EQUALS `compensation is not recoverable: notice was not given as s 254(1) requires, and no special circumstance applies`

-- =====================================================================================================================
-- CASE W13. The time for a claim (1998 Act s 261).
-- =====================================================================================================================

-- Injured 15 March 2025: claim by 15 September 2025. Injured 31 August 2025: 6 months later has no 31st, so 28 February
-- 2026 (READING). Injured 1 March 2025 but first aware on 1 February 2026: from awareness, 1 August 2026 (s 261(6)).
#ASSERT `By what day must I make my claim` `15 Mar 2025` `15 Mar 2025` EQUALS `15 Sep 2025`
#ASSERT `By what day must I make my claim` `31 Aug 2025` `31 Aug 2025` EQUALS `28 Feb 2026`
#ASSERT `By what day must I make my claim` `1 Mar 2025` `1 Feb 2026` EQUALS `1 Aug 2026`
-- Answers: death claim; injury day; aware day; claim day; worker's own claim in time; reasonable cause; death or serious
-- and permanent disablement; insurer accepted; Authority approved.
#ASSERT `Is my claim in time` FALSE `15 Mar 2025` `15 Mar 2025` `15 Sep 2025` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `made in time: within 6 months (s 261(1))`
#ASSERT `Is my claim in time` FALSE `15 Mar 2025` `15 Mar 2025` `16 Sep 2025` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `late, and compensation cannot be recovered (s 261(1))`
#ASSERT `Is my claim in time` FALSE `15 Mar 2025` `15 Mar 2025` `16 Sep 2025` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `late, but no bar: reasonable cause, and made within 3 years (s 261(4)(a))`
-- 15 March 2028 is the last day of the 3 years; 16 March 2028 is outside.
#ASSERT `Is my claim in time` FALSE `15 Mar 2025` `15 Mar 2025` `15 Mar 2028` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `late, but no bar: reasonable cause, and made within 3 years (s 261(4)(a))`
#ASSERT `Is my claim in time` FALSE `15 Mar 2025` `15 Mar 2025` `16 Mar 2028` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `late, and compensation cannot be recovered (s 261(1))`
#ASSERT `Is my claim in time` FALSE `15 Mar 2025` `15 Mar 2025` `16 Mar 2028` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `late, but no bar: reasonable cause, and the injury resulted in death or serious and permanent disablement (s 261(4)(b))`
-- No reasonable cause, but the insurer accepts: within 3 years it may (s 261(5)); after 3 years only with approval.
#ASSERT `Is my claim in time` FALSE `15 Mar 2025` `15 Mar 2025` `16 Sep 2025` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `late, but no bar: the insurer determined to accept it (s 261(5))`
#ASSERT `Is my claim in time` FALSE `15 Mar 2025` `15 Mar 2025` `16 Mar 2028` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `late, and compensation cannot be recovered (s 261(1))`
#ASSERT `Is my claim in time` FALSE `15 Mar 2025` `15 Mar 2025` `16 Mar 2028` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `late, but no bar: the insurer determined to accept it (s 261(5))`
-- A claim for a death on 1 February 2026, made on 1 August 2026: within 6 months of the death (s 261(1)).
#ASSERT `Is my claim in time` TRUE `1 Feb 2026` `1 Feb 2026` `1 Aug 2026` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `made in time: within 6 months (s 261(1))`
-- A claim for a death on 1 July 2025, made 7 months later on 1 February 2026: late, but the worker had claimed for the
-- injury in time (s 261(2)); without that, barred.
#ASSERT `Is my claim in time` TRUE `1 Jul 2025` `1 Jul 2025` `1 Feb 2026` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `in time: the worker's own claim was made in time (s 261(2))`
#ASSERT `Is my claim in time` TRUE `1 Jul 2025` `1 Jul 2025` `1 Feb 2026` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `late, and compensation cannot be recovered (s 261(1))`

-- =====================================================================================================================
-- CASE W14. Deadlines the employer and the insurer must meet (1998 Act ss 264(1), 267, 268, 274).
-- =====================================================================================================================

-- s 264(1): claim received 3 November 2026: forward by 10 November.
#ASSERT `Has my employer missed the deadline to forward my claim` FALSE `3 Nov 2026` TRUE `10 Nov 2026` `12 Nov 2026` EQUALS `done in time`
#ASSERT `Has my employer missed the deadline to forward my claim` FALSE `3 Nov 2026` TRUE `11 Nov 2026` `12 Nov 2026` EQUALS `done late: the deadline was` `10 Nov 2026`
#ASSERT `Has my employer missed the deadline to forward my claim` FALSE `3 Nov 2026` FALSE `3 Nov 2026` `9 Nov 2026` EQUALS `not yet done, and the deadline has not passed: it is` `10 Nov 2026`
#ASSERT `Has my employer missed the deadline to forward my claim` FALSE `3 Nov 2026` FALSE `3 Nov 2026` `11 Nov 2026` EQUALS `missed: not done by the deadline` `10 Nov 2026`
#ASSERT `Has my employer missed the deadline to forward my claim` TRUE `3 Nov 2026` FALSE `3 Nov 2026` `11 Nov 2026` EQUALS `no such duty`
-- ss 267, 268: initial notification 2 November 2026: 7 days to 9 November.
#ASSERT `Has the insurer missed its 7-day deadline` `2 Nov 2026` TRUE `6 Nov 2026` FALSE `2 Nov 2026` `12 Nov 2026` EQUALS `done in time`
#ASSERT `Has the insurer missed its 7-day deadline` `2 Nov 2026` FALSE `2 Nov 2026` TRUE `9 Nov 2026` `12 Nov 2026` EQUALS `done in time`
#ASSERT `Has the insurer missed its 7-day deadline` `2 Nov 2026` FALSE `2 Nov 2026` FALSE `2 Nov 2026` `12 Nov 2026` EQUALS `missed: not done by the deadline` `9 Nov 2026`
#ASSERT `Has the insurer missed its 7-day deadline` `2 Nov 2026` TRUE `12 Nov 2026` FALSE `2 Nov 2026` `12 Nov 2026` EQUALS `done late: the deadline was` `9 Nov 2026`
-- s 274: claim for weekly payments made 2 November 2026: 21 days to 23 November.
#ASSERT `Has the insurer missed its deadline to decide my weekly payments claim` `2 Nov 2026` 0 `2 Nov 2026` TRUE `20 Nov 2026` `24 Nov 2026` EQUALS `done in time`
#ASSERT `Has the insurer missed its deadline to decide my weekly payments claim` `2 Nov 2026` 0 `2 Nov 2026` FALSE `2 Nov 2026` `20 Nov 2026` EQUALS `not yet done, and the deadline has not passed: it is` `23 Nov 2026`
#ASSERT `Has the insurer missed its deadline to decide my weekly payments claim` `2 Nov 2026` 0 `2 Nov 2026` FALSE `2 Nov 2026` `24 Nov 2026` EQUALS `missed: not done by the deadline` `23 Nov 2026`
-- Provisional acceptance for 12 weeks from 5 November 2026: 84 days later, 28 January 2027 (s 274(2), (3)).
#ASSERT `Has the insurer missed its deadline to decide my weekly payments claim` `2 Nov 2026` 12 `5 Nov 2026` FALSE `2 Nov 2026` `24 Nov 2026` EQUALS `not yet done, and the deadline has not passed: it is` `28 Jan 2027`

